message.content:
The `elf_cvt_note` function also has the fix:
```c
/* Copy over any leftover data unconverted.  Probably part of
   truncated name/desc data.  */
if (unlikely (len > 0) && src != dest)
    memcpy (dest, src, len);
```

So `ELF_T_NHDR` and `ELF_T_NHDR8` are also fixed.

That leaves `ELF_T_GNUHASH` (SHT_GNU_HASH) for ELFCLASS64, which uses `elf_cvt_gnuhash`. Let me check if `elf_cvt_gnuhash` has the fix.

